{"name":"Sky Magenta","hex":"#cf71af","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"},{"term":"magenta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color which is close to the equal mixture of red and blue which is an additive secondary color but a subtractive primary color evoked by the combination of red and light blue."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the color of fuchsia, fuchsine, light purple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magenta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of magenta","blocks":[{"text":"The color magenta has notable tints and shades. These various colors are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Color_icon_magenta.svg/330px-Color_icon_magenta.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_magenta","wikidata":"Q17079435"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Magenta","blocks":[{"text":"Magenta is a purplish-pink color. On color wheels of the RGB and CMYK color models, it is located directly midway between blue and red. It is one of the four colors of subtractive ink used in color printing by most color printers, also known as CMYK along with yellow, cyan, and black to make all the other colors and hues. The tone of magenta used in printing, printer's magenta, is redder than the magenta of the RGB (additive) model, the former being closer to rose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Pink_swanboat_hosting_a_real_bird_on_its_head%2C_on_Shinobazu_Pond%2C_Ueno_Park%2C_Tokyo.jpg/330px-Pink_swanboat_hosting_a_real_bird_on_its_head%2C_on_Shinobazu_Pond%2C_Ueno_Park%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magenta","wikidata":"Q3276756"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Line_of_purples.png/500px-Line_of_purples.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Line_of_purples.png/500px-Line_of_purples.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The most saturated magentas that humans are able to perceive lie on the line of purples, which connects violet and red in the chromaticity diagram","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALine_of_purples.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/RGB_combination_on_wall.png/500px-RGB_combination_on_wall.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/RGB_combination_on_wall.png/1280px-RGB_combination_on_wall.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/RGB_combination_on_wall.png/500px-RGB_combination_on_wall.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red, green and blue lights, representing the three basic additive primary colors of the RGB color system, red, green, and blue. Magenta light is composed of equal amounts of red and blue light.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARGB_combination_on_wall.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Purple_African_Violet_Top.JPG/500px-Purple_African_Violet_Top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Purple_African_Violet_Top.JPG/500px-Purple_African_Violet_Top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APurple_African_Violet_Top.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Amaranth_%28231529041%29.jpeg/500px-Amaranth_%28231529041%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Amaranth_%28231529041%29.jpeg/1280px-Amaranth_%28231529041%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Amaranth_%28231529041%29.jpeg